the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:

*a benefit* is in order towards *an actor* who felt provoked into *an action* by *a person* s non-aggressive attitude.

the knowledge base includes:

scenario standard is:
    leniency is in order towards a criminal who felt provoked into raping by a victim s non-aggressive attitude.
    leniency is in order towards a criminal who felt provoked into killing by a victim s non-aggressive attitude.

    one expects ["leniency is in order towards _ who felt provoked into raping by _ s non-aggressive attitude", "leniency is in order towards _ who felt provoked into killing by _ s non-aggressive attitude"].

scenario no standard is:
    leniency is in order towards a rapist who felt provoked into raping by a victim s non-aggressive attitude if
        the rapist is a man
        and the victim is a woman.
    person1 is a man.
    person2 is a woman. 
    one expects ["leniency is in order towards person1 who felt provoked into raping by person2 s non-aggressive attitude"]. 

query one is:
    which benefit is in order towards which person who felt provoked into which action by which other person s non-aggressive attitude. 